    <briefdescription>
<para>The structure represents a passport of a member. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>It consists of some vital necessary member attributes, allowing to detect its state, exact address. The whole passport is necessary for each info related to a member: for anti-entropy records, for dissemination events. The components can inherit that structure and add more attributes. Or just encode new attributes after the passport. For example, anti-entropy can add a payload when it is up to date; dissemination adds a payload when it is up to date and TTD is &gt; 0. </para>    </detaileddescription>
